{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced the ResNet50 image encoder with an ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (imagenet_vit_l) while holding all other settings constant (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted fusion), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.706 and F1 of 0.667, a ~2.8-point accuracy improvement over the identical pipeline with ResNet50 (0.678 acc / 0.646 F1). Because only the image encoder was changed, the gain is cleanly attributable to the encoder, confirming that a stronger, more expressive visual representation extracts meaningfully more complementary signal beyond what ResNet50 captures and further justifying continued investment in the image modality. It remains uncertain whether the ~0.706 accuracy approaches a practical ceiling for this task, whether alternative fusion strategies (e.g., attention-based) could yield further gains, or whether even stronger image encoders would continue to produce incremental improvements."
}

